-- title:
--   Formal smoothness of the descended supersingular chart at q=3
-- statement:
--   **Setting and constants.** Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (the hypothesis `hA`, i.e. `LiesOverPrime`), let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, write $O$ for the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ obtained by pulling $A$ back along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$. The constants hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres`, `hκ` require that $O$ be a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that $O$ be Henselian, that the residue field of $O$ be algebraically closed, and that every $a \in A$ be congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Level, function field and chart algebra.** Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be the subgroup $H_1 = \mathrm{levelH}(q,M') \sqcap \ker\big((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times\big)$ (`hH₁`), where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, so $H_1$ consists of the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ and modulo $\ell_g$. Let $K_\ell$ be an intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)/k_0$, equipped with an $O$-algebra structure compatible with the tower $O \to k_0 \to K_\ell$, and assume (`hKℓ`) that $K_\ell$ is the field generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansions of the modular functions of level $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$, i.e. $K_\ell = \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}(q^2M',H_1))$. Let $j_\ell \in K_\ell$ be nonzero and equal to the coefficientwise image $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,(\mathsf{jq})$ of the classical $q$-expansion of $j$ (`hjℓ`). The relevant chart algebra is `chartAlgFin O K_ℓ j_ℓ`, the subalgebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $O[j_\ell]$. Let $\xi \in k_0$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hξ`). Further data: $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q \in K_\ell$ (`hjK`), this element lies in the chart algebra (`hjC`), and $a_0 \in O$ with $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q - a_0 \in y$ (`ha₀y`), where $y$ is the maximal ideal described below.
--
--   **Places and constant reduction.** Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over the residue field of $A$, and $s \in W$. The hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of supersingular places: those places $w$ that are rational (the structure map to the residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value at the geometric $j$-generator lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)`, i.e. is a $j$-invariant all of whose elliptic curves have no nontrivial $q$-torsion. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the function field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A,M')$ (a valuation subring `integers` of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal of `integers`, compatibility of `integers` and of the residue map with $A$ and its residue map, an existence-of-scaling clause, and a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with orders). The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of the given series.
--
--   **Auxiliary scalars.** Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$, let $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and let $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lie in $A$ and satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`); $\varpi_t' \in O$ is the same element (`hϖt'`). Let $K_b$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$ (`hKb`), $A_b$ a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements lying in $A$ (`hAb`), and $\varpi_b \in A_b$ nonzero generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$. Tameness (`htame`): the image of $\ell_g - 1$ in $O$ is a unit.
--
--   **The point $y$.** Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of `chartAlgFin O K_ℓ j_ℓ` containing the image of $\pi_0$ (`hy`, `hϖy`). Supersingularity (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from the chart algebra to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_\ell)$ lies in `ssJSet q Ω`. Localisation over $s$ (`hover`): for every $g$ in the full level-$M'$ modular function field whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, which is regular at every place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ at which $j$ is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every element $c$ of $k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference between $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g$ (assumed to lie in $K_\ell$ and in the chart algebra) and $c$ lies in $y$. Transitivity on the fibre (`hOrbit`): every maximal ideal $y'$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ and satisfying the same localisation condition over $s$ is carried onto $y$ by a level automorphism, namely there are $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau : K_\ell \simeq_{k_0} K_\ell$ with `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q^2*M') H₁ γ⁻¹ Kℓ τ` (the $q$-expansion identity characterising the automorphism induced by $\gamma$ on level-$\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ modular functions) such that $\tau$ preserves the chart algebra and $f \in y \iff \tau f \in y'$ on it.
--
--   **The rigid affine chart.** Let $B_t$ be an $O$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ and $W_t$ a valuation subring of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$ (`hBW`). The hypothesis `hS1` (fourteen clauses, summarised here) requires: the chart algebra is contained in $B_t$; $K_\ell$ is the fraction field of $B_t$; $B_t$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $O$; $B_t/(\pi_0)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; the elements of $k_0$ lying in $W_t$ are exactly those of $O$; the maximal ideal of $W_t$ is generated by $\pi_0$ and $W_t$ is a discrete valuation ring; $y$ is the contraction of the maximal ideal of $W_t$ to the chart algebra, and $W_t$ is the localisation of $B_t$ at that maximal ideal; for every algebra structure of the field `GaloisField q 2` on the residue field of $O$ there is a surjective homomorphism $\rho$ from $B_t$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField O)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) whose vanishing locus is the maximal ideal of $W_t$, compatible with reduction on constants, and equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W_t$, through a scalar $c$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c) \in$ [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325), with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$, and with the pair $(1,c)$ realised by a further level automorphism; $B_t$ is stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$; every prime of $B_t$ containing $\pi_0$ is obtained from the maximal locus of $W_t$ by such an automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; and an element of $B_t$ sent into the maximal ideal of $W_t$ by all these automorphisms is divisible by $\pi_0$.
--
--   **Inertia and ends.** Let $n \ge 1$ with $n \mid q+1$ (`hn1`, `hnq`) and $n = 2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$ (`hn`), where `placeWidthChar` is `jWidthChar q` of the value of $s$ at the geometric $j$-generator divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; for $q=3$ the numerator is $6$ if that value is $0$ and $1$ otherwise. Let $\gamma_0 \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and let $\tau_0$ be a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ preserving $W_t$ (`hτ₀`, `hτ₀W`). Let $m \ge 1$ with $\pi_0^m = \varpi_t' w$ for some unit $w$ of $O$ (`hm`), and let $\zeta_c$ in the $\pi_0$-adic completion of $O$ satisfy $\zeta_c^n = 1$ with $\zeta_c^k - 1$ a unit for $0 < k < n$ (`hζc`, `hζcprim`). Let `ends` be a finite set of subrings of $K_\ell$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hR7` (twelve clauses, summarised here) requires: $\tau_0^n$ fixes $B_t$ pointwise while $\tau_0^k$ moves some element of $B_t$ for $0<k<n$; every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W_t$ agrees on $B_t$ with some $\tau_0^k$, $k<n$; `ends` has $q+1$ elements; the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma_0(M')$ that preserve $W_t$ permute `ends`, transitively; each end is $\tau_0$-stable; distinct ends are separated by an element that is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other; there is an $O$-subalgebra $B_c$ of finite type, stable under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, contained in every end, with each end the localisation of $B_c$ at its units; an automorphism carrying some end into $W_t$ preserves $W_t$; each end $O'$ is contained in $W_t$, is local and Noetherian, contains the chart algebra, meets $k_0$ exactly in $O$, has every element non-unit-congruent to a constant, and carries the crossing-model data: $\pi_0 \in O'$, elements $c_x, c_y$, a unit $u$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $O'$ with `UVCrossingModel` over the $\pi_0$-adic completion of $O$ at parameter $\pi_0^m$, units $\gamma_U, \gamma_V$, an automorphism $\theta_0$ and an inverse $\zeta_c'$ of $\zeta_c$, such that $c_xc_y = \pi_0^m u$, $\iota$ sends constants to `UVCrossingModel.const`, $\iota(c_x) = \gamma_U\,\mathrm{U}$ and $\iota(c_y) = \gamma_V\,\mathrm{V}$, $c_y$ lies in and $c_x$ lies outside the maximal ideal of $W_t$, $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q - a_0$ lies in $O'$ with $\iota$-image $w_V \mathrm{V}^e$ for a unit $w_V$ and some $e \ge 1$, $\iota$ intertwines $\tau_0$ with $\theta_0$, and $\theta_0(\mathrm U) - \zeta_c \mathrm U$ and $\theta_0(\mathrm V) - \zeta_c' \mathrm V$ lie in the square of the maximal ideal; together with a valuation subring $W_x$ of $K_\ell$ containing $O'$ and the chart algebra, meeting $k_0$ in $O$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, admitting an element $t$ and also $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$ with the property that a polynomial over $O$ whose value there lies in the maximal ideal has all coefficients in the maximal ideal of $O$, with $c_x$ inside and $c_y$ outside the maximal ideal of $W_x$, with chart-algebra elements in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ lying in $y$ and some element of $y$ outside it, with every other end containing an element outside $W_x$, and with $O'$ the only end mapped into $W_x$ by a level automorphism; and a subalgebra $B_x$ of finite type contained in $B_t \cap O'$, stable under those level automorphisms, whose elements are regular at every place at which $j_\ell$ is, with $O'$ the localisation of $B_x$ at the units of $O'$, and containing an element escaping every valuation subring that meets $k_0$ in $O$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, admits no monic polynomial value at $j_\ell$ in its maximal ideal, and fails to contain some element of $O'$. The last clause of `hR7` states that for every valuation subring $V$ of $K_\ell$ meeting $k_0$ exactly in $O$, containing the chart algebra and with $y$ inside the maximal ideal of $V$, either $B_t \subseteq V$ or there is an end all of whose elements lie in $V$, the non-units going into the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hR9` provides an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring $V$ that meets $k_0$ in $O$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, and contains $j_\ell$ with no monic polynomial over $O$ taking a value at $j_\ell$ in the maximal ideal of $V$. The hypothesis `hR10` provides, for every maximal ideal $y''$ of the chart algebra containing $\pi_0$ that is not matched with $y$ by any level automorphism attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, an element of $B_t$ lying outside every valuation subring containing the chart algebra in which the elements whose $\tau^{-1}$-image lies in $y''$ are in the maximal ideal.
--
--   **The descent data.** Let $G$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ (`hG`), let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$ (`hK₀`), let $B_0$ be the $O$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ consisting of the elements of $B_t$ fixed by every $\tau \in G$ (`hB₀`), and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ whose members are the elements lying in $W_t$ (`hW₀'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** The algebra $B_0$ is formally smooth over $O = A \cap k_0$.
--
--   This is the formal smoothness clause for the chart of the semistable model obtained by descending the rigid supersingular chart $(B_t, W_t)$ along the finite group $G$ of level automorphisms, in the $q = 3$, $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-guard frame of the analysis of the reduction of modular curves at a supersingular point. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.AuxLevel.supersingularDVR_affineChart_invariants_of_rigidChart_linkedScalars_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.AuxLevel.supersingularDVR_affineChart_invariants_of_rigidChart_linkedScalars_of_eq_three_of_dvd), where the descended chart is assembled with its discrete valuation data.
